{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_actions

    The three decisions, rendered into a core sticky footer by the renderer.

    Only the decisions live here. A core sticky footer is a fixed box whose content area clips
    with no scrollbar, so the message box and the two choosers stay in the page body - the same
    split the queue's own bar makes, for the same reason.

    Each button carries name formaction and its own value, so the button pressed IS the decision
    taken and manage.php reads it with optional_param. It must stay a form CONTROL rather than
    the HTML5 formaction attribute, which would post nothing under that name.

    The destructive decision is first in source order and pushed to the far edge by this row's
    OWN justify-content-between - not the footer's, which applies its classes to a content area
    whose only child is this row and therefore had nothing to spread.

    Being first also makes Cancel the form's DEFAULT submit, which is what an operator pressing
    Enter in a chooser gets. That is deliberate and it is safe only because manage.php intercepts
    formaction cancel and asks: whichever button comes first inherits the default, so no ordering
    makes both safe, and the interception is what makes this one safe. The two hold together -
    reordering these buttons without moving the interception restores the original hazard, that
    Enter in a chooser silently enrols the applicant.

    The row does not wrap. The bar is a fixed 80px box whose content area clips with no
    scrollbar, so a wrapped second line is painted where nobody can see it; below the width the
    three labels need, the row scrolls sideways instead.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * actions array - one entry per decision, each with:
      * value string - what travels as formaction
      * label string - the button's text
      * style string - the Bootstrap button class it carries

    Example context (json):
    {
        "actions": [
            {"value": "cancel", "label": "Cancel this application", "style": "btn-outline-danger"},
            {"value": "wait", "label": "Defer this application", "style": "btn-secondary"},
            {"value": "confirm", "label": "Confirm this application", "style": "btn-primary"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-reviewactions d-flex flex-nowrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-2 w-100">
    {{#actions}}
        <button type="submit" name="formaction" value="{{value}}" class="btn {{style}}">
            {{label}}
        </button>
    {{/actions}}
</div>
